      "errorMessage": "<task id=\"ses_f074c468fffeivh1IpO7amo0Yf\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nI now have a complete picture. Here is my report.\n\n---\n\n# How twenty-front detects installed apps and gates native UI\n\n## 1. Hooks / states / selectors for \"is this app installed\"\n\nThere is **no generic `useIsApplicationInstalled` hook**. Install state is centralized in the metadata store and read in three ways.\n\n### The canonical install-state source: `applicationsSelector`\n\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/applications/states/applicationsSelector.ts` (lines 5-12) returns the `FlatApplication[]` held under the `'applications'` metadata-store key:\n\n```ts\nexport const applicationsSelector = createAtomSelector<FlatApplication[]>({\n  key: 'applicationsSelector',\n  get: ({ get }) => {\n    const storeItem = get(metadataStoreState, 'applications');\n    return storeItem.current as FlatApplication[];\n  },\n});\n```\n\nThe `'applications'` key is registered in `metadataStoreState.ts` (`ALL_METADATA_ENTITY_KEYS`, line 37). Each `FlatApplication` carries a `universalIdentifier` (see below).\n\n### Populated by `ApplicationsLoadEffect`\n\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/applications/components/ApplicationsLoadEffect.tsx` queries `FindManyApplications` and maps each row into a `FlatApplication`, then writes it into the store (lines 90-102):\n\n```ts\nconst applications: FlatApplication[] =\n  result.data.findManyApplications.map((application) => ({\n    id: application.id,\n    universalIdentifier: application.universalIdentifier,\n    name: application.name,\n    description: application.description,\n    version: application.version,\n    state: application.state,\n    applicationRegistrationId: application.applicationRegistrationId,\n  }));\n\nreplaceDraft('applications', applications);\napplyChanges();\n```\n\nNote this effect is gated on the `APPLICATIONS` permission flag and skipped on auth/onboarding pages (lines 49-51). So on onboarding, the store may be empty.\n\n### `useInstalledApplications` — the closest thing to a generic hook\n\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/applications/hooks/useInstalledApplications.ts` (lines 9-33) merges the store's applications with a fresh `FindManyApplications` query (for logo/registration), and refetches on app lifecycle events. It returns `ApplicationWithoutRelation[]` — the installed set for the current workspace. You filter it by `universalIdentifier` or `name`.\n\n### The A2E-specific filtered hook: `useA2eSuiteApplications`\n\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/a2e-workspace/hooks/useA2eSuiteApplications.ts` (lines 15-57) queries `FindManyApplications` directly and splits into `installedApplications` (filtered to the A2E allowlist) and `availableApplications` (catalog minus installed). Key excerpt:\n\n```ts\nconst installedUniversalIdentifiers = useMemo(\n  () => new Set((data?.findManyApplications ?? []).map((a) => a.universalIdentifier)),\n  [data],\n);\nconst installedApplications = useMemo(\n  () =>\n    (data?.findManyApplications ?? []).filter((application) =>\n      A2E_SUITE_APPLICATION_UNIVERSAL_IDENTIFIERS.includes(application.universalIdentifier),\n    ),\n  [data],\n);\n```\n\n### `useIsThirdPartyApplication` — per-application check keyed on `applicationId`\n\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/applications/hooks/useIsThirdPartyApplication.ts` (lines 7-25) resolves the app from `currentWorkspace.installedApplications` by `id`:\n\n```ts\nconst application = currentWorkspace?.installedApplications.find(\n  (app) => app.id === applicationId,\n);\nreturn isDefined(application) && !isTwentyStandardApplication(application) &&\n  !isWorkspaceCustomApplication(application, currentWorkspace);\n```\n\nThis is used by the command-menu renderer (section 4).\n\n### `useApplicationByUniversalIdentifier` (not present under that name)\n\nThere is **no `useApplicationByUniversalIdentifier` hook**. The universal-identifier lookup exists only as GraphQL documents:\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/applications/graphql/queries/findOneApplicationByUniversalIdentifier.ts` (lines 4-7)\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/applications/graphql/queries/findOneApplicationSummary.ts`\n\nUsed in `pages/settings/applications/SettingsAvailableApplicationDetails.tsx` (lines 37, 63). Not a reactive install-state hook.\n\n### `useFilteredObjectMetadataItems` — object-metadata filtering (not app filtering)\n\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-metadata/hooks/useFilteredObjectMetadataItems.ts` reads `objectMetadataItemsWithFieldsSelector` and exposes `activeObjectMetadataItems`, `activeNonSystemObjectMetadataItems`, `findActiveObjectMetadataItemByNamePlural`, etc. (lines 5-68). This is object-level, not app-install-level, but it is the closest \"what does this workspace have\" selector and is widely used.\n\n`useObjectMetadataItems` (`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-metadata/hooks/useObjectMetadataItems.ts`, lines 4-13) returns the raw `objectMetadataItems` array — this is what the home-dashboard widgets use for gating.\n\n### `applicationMetadataItems` / `applicationState`\n\n- No selector named `applicationMetadataItems` exists. The metadata-store key is `'applications'` (plural), surfaced by `applicationsSelector`.\n- `applicationState` exists only as the GraphQL enum `ApplicationState` on the `Application` type (generated graphql), not as a front Jotai state.\n\n---\n\n## 2. A2E app universal identifier constants and the drift guard\n\n### `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/a2e-workspace/constants/A2eSuiteApplicationUniversalIdentifiers.ts`\n\nFull content (20 lines):\n\n```ts\n// Universal identifiers mirror application.config.ts in each\n// packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-* app; they are committed forever there,\n// so listing them here is safe drift-free data, not a second source of truth\n// for identity.\nexport const A2E_SUITE_APPLICATION_UNIVERSAL_IDENTIFIERS: string[] = [\n  // a2e-documents\n  '19126a9c-7cc0-4368-aaba-c7e5a87b0c48',\n  // a2e-accounting (Bilan)\n  'b11a0000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001',\n  // a2e-projects\n  '4f759655-84f8-434d-9c76-ee1850e8c1a4',\n  // a2e-chat\n  'e2dce399-87f1-4548-b307-5f368b4d5dd4',\n  // a2e-drive\n  'b11cd01f-75de-4acd-8e67-0e9c484fde02',\n  // a2e-crm\n  'c31e0000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000',\n  // a2e-links\n  '895bb7aa-3ae3-400f-9dfa-72116f0021e2',\n];\n```\n\n`a2e-links` = `895bb7aa-3ae3-400f-9dfa-72116f0021e2` (confirmed in `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-links/src/constants/universal-identifiers.ts`, line 16).\n\n### Related constants\n\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/a2e-workspace/constants/A2eSuiteApplicationGroupHeadings.ts` (lines 6-9) — maps a universal identifier to a Cmd+K group heading (`a2e-projects` → `'Bureau'`).\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/onboarding/constants/OnboardingInstallableApps.ts` (lines 4-55) — the onboarding install list with labels/descriptions; includes all seven A2E apps plus three third-party ones.\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/quick-capture/utils/newPageDocument.ts` (lines 1-5) — a **duplicate local copy** of the a2e-documents identifier, with a comment explaining the constants file allows a single const per file:\n  ```ts\n  export const A2E_DOCUMENTS_APPLICATION_UNIVERSAL_IDENTIFIER =\n    '19126a9c-7cc0-4368-aaba-c7e5a87b0c48';\n  ```\n\n### The drift-guard spec\n\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/a2e-workspace/constants/__tests__/A2eSuiteApplicationUniversalIdentifiers.test.ts` (133 lines). It reads the real app sources from `packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-*` — parsing `/src/application.config.ts` or `/src/constants/universal-identifiers.ts` with:\n\n```ts\nconst APPLICATION_UNIVERSAL_IDENTIFIER_PATTERN =\n  /export const APPLICATION_UNIVERSAL_IDENTIFIER\\s*=\\s*'([0-9a-f-]{36})'/;\n```\n\nIt then asserts four things (lines 86-133):\n1. discovers exactly the seven first-party apps (`a2e-accounting`, `a2e-chat`, `a2e-crm`, `a2e-documents`, `a2e-drive`, `a2e-links`, `a2e-projects`);\n2. `A2E_SUITE_APPLICATION_UNIVERSAL_IDENTIFIERS` lists each of them exactly once (no duplicates) and has the same length;\n3. every first-party app is offered by `ONBOARDING_INSTALLABLE_APPS`;\n4. every first-party app is both `COPY`'d into the Dockerfile and present in the Dockerfile build-loop `for app in ...;` list.\n\nA related drift test is `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/a2e-workspace/constants/__tests__/A2eSuiteApplicationGroupHeadings.test.ts`.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Gating native code on an app-owned object existing\n\n### The util\n\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/home-dashboard/utils/hasObjectMetadataItem.ts` (14 lines, full):\n\n```ts\nexport type ObjectMetadataNameHolder = {\n  nameSingular: string;\n};\n\n// Apps install as a unit, so one object metadata item is the install signal a\n// widget gates on: calling `useFindManyRecords` for an absent app object throws\n// ObjectMetadataItemNotFoundError before its `skip` flag is ever read.\nexport const hasObjectMetadataItem = (\n  objectMetadataItems: ObjectMetadataNameHolder[],\n  nameSingular: string,\n): boolean =>\n  objectMetadataItems.some(\n    (objectMetadataItem) => objectMetadataItem.nameSingular === nameSingular,\n  );\n```\n\n### Usage example (M11b home-dashboard)\n\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/home-dashboard/components/RecentPagesWidget.tsx` (lines 15-29):\n\n```ts\nconst DOCUMENT_OBJECT_NAME_SINGULAR = 'document';\n\n// Bureau owns the `document` object, so the card self-gates: when the app is\n// absent the fetch is never reached and the widget shows its empty state.\nexport const RecentPagesWidget = () => {\n  const { objectMetadataItems } = useObjectMetadataItems();\n\n  if (!hasObjectMetadataItem(objectMetadataItems, DOCUMENT_OBJECT_NAME_SINGULAR)) {\n    return <RecentPagesWidgetContent entries={[]} />;\n  }\n\n  return <RecentPagesRecords />;\n};\n```\n\nThe pattern is a **two-component split**: the wrapper checks object metadata and only renders the component that calls `useFindManyRecords` once the object is present. Same pattern in `PendingBilanWidget.tsx` (lines 25-38), which gates on `invoice` (`BILAN_INVOICE_OBJECT_NAME_SINGULAR`).\n\nThe companion unit test: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/home-dashboard/utils/__tests__/hasObjectMetadataItem.test.ts`.\n\nAn alternative gate by universal identifier exists in quick-capture: `newPageDocument.ts` lines 7-22 defines `isDocumentApplicationInstalled(...)`, with the comment explaining why it prefers the identifier over probing object metadata:\n\n> the host can only create it once the app's metadata is installed, so every new-page entry-point is gated on this identifier rather than probing object metadata (which can resolve while an install is still mid-flight).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Checking whether an app-contributed command menu item / front component is available\n\n### Front components: no dedicated \"is available\" check — they come from metadata\n\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/front-components/states/frontComponentsSelector.ts` (lines 5-14) simply returns the `'frontComponents'` metadata-store key. There is no front-side predicate beyond presence in that array (which the server populates from installed apps).\n\n### Command menu items: appear from metadata; there is no per-item availability hook\n\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/command-menu-item/states/commandMenuItemsSelector.ts` (lines 8-35) reads `'commandMenuItems'`, keeps `item.isActive`, and joins in the `frontComponent` by `frontComponentId`. So a command-menu item contributed by an app **simply appears once the app is installed** (its rows are synced into the metadata store). There is no `useCommandMenuItemAvailability`-style gate; the gating is the app's own install state upstream.\n\nWhat the renderer does with an app-owned item is a **presentation** distinction, not availability: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/command-menu-item/display/components/CommandMenuItemRenderer.tsx` (lines 115-146) calls `useIsThirdPartyApplication(item.applicationId)` and, when true, renders `<AppMenuItem>` (with the app chip) instead of the standard `CommandMenuItem`:\n\n```ts\nconst isThirdPartyApp = useIsThirdPartyApplication(item.applicationId);\n...\nif (isThirdPartyApp) {\n  return (\n    <SelectableListItem itemId={item.id} onEnter={onItemClick}>\n      <AppMenuItem applicationId={item.applicationId} text={label} ... />\n    </SelectableListItem>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n`AppMenuItem` (`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/applications/components/AppMenuItem.tsx`, lines 15-41) resolves the app chip via `useApplicationChipData`.\n\nThe command-menu item fragment carries `universalIdentifier` and `applicationId`: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/command-menu-item/graphql/fragments/commandMenuItemFragment.ts` (lines 6-7).\n\n**Contrast — native (host) command items are gated explicitly.** The \"New page\" quick-capture command is *native code*, so it checks the app identifier itself: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/quick-capture/hooks/useNewPageCommand.ts` (lines 9-25):\n\n```ts\nconst isDocumentApplicationInstalled = useIsDocumentApplicationInstalled();\n...\nconst shouldDisplayNewPageCommand =\n  isDocumentApplicationInstalled &&\n  normalizeSearchText(newPageCommandLabel).includes(normalizeSearchText(sidePanelSearch.trim()));\n```\n\nwith `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/quick-capture/hooks/useIsDocumentApplicationInstalled.ts` (lines 6-16) reading `applicationsSelector` and testing `universalIdentifier`. So: **app-contributed items appear automatically when installed; native host items gate themselves on the app universal identifier.**\n\n---\n\n## 5. The `a2eLink` object and querying/creating app-object records from native front code\n\n### Object identity\n\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-links/src/objects/a2e-link.object.ts` (lines 14-23):\n\n```ts\nexport default defineObject({\n  universalIdentifier: OBJECT_IDS.a2eLink,   // c31f0100-0000-4000-8000-000000000000\n  nameSingular: 'a2eLink',\n  namePlural: 'a2eLinks',\n  ...\n```\n\nSo native front code addresses it by `objectNameSingular: 'a2eLink'`. There is currently **no `a2eLink` reference anywhere in `packages/twenty-front/src`** (grep found only the app package and the comment in `A2eSuiteApplicationUniversalIdentifiers.ts`). Existing native A2E code uses `document` / `invoice` / `savedSubvention` instead.\n\n### The three standard hooks\n\n**`useObjectMetadataItem`** — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-metadata/hooks/useObjectMetadataItem.ts` (lines 10-35). This is the crux of the behavior: it reads `objectMetadataItemFamilySelector` and **throws** when the object is absent:\n\n```ts\nif (!isDefined(objectMetadataItem)) {\n  throw new ObjectMetadataItemNotFoundError(objectNameSingular, objectMetadataItems);\n}\n```\n\nError class: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-metadata/errors/ObjectMetadataNotFoundError.ts` (lines 3-15).\n\n**`useFindManyRecords`** — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/hooks/useFindManyRecords.ts` (lines 36-104). It calls `useObjectMetadataItem` at line 49 (throwing if absent), builds the query, then *also* guards the Apollo `skip` at line 95:\n\n```ts\nskip: skip || !isDefined(objectMetadataItem) || !hasReadPermission,\n```\n\nBecause the `useObjectMetadataItem` throw happens before the `skip` is read, **the `skip` flag does not protect you from an uninstalled object** — this is exactly the reason the home-dashboard util exists (see the comment in `hasObjectMetadataItem.ts`). Usage example: `RecentPagesWidget.tsx` lines 34-39.\n\n**`useCreateOneRecord`** — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/hooks/useCreateOneRecord.ts` (lines 42-77). It calls `useObjectMetadataItem` at line 54, so it too throws for a missing object before any mutation. The returned `createOneRecord` (line 84) does optimistic cache creation, mutation, and aggregate refetch, and throws `CustomError('Failed to create record')` if the mutation returns nothing (lines 212-214).\n\n### Native usage pattern (host creates an app-owned record)\n\nThe existing example is quick-capture creating a Bureau `document`:\n\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/quick-capture/hooks/useCreateNewPage.ts` (lines 14-42):\n\n```ts\nexport const useCreateNewPage = () => {\n  const { createOneRecord } = useCreateOneRecord({\n    objectNameSingular: DOCUMENT_OBJECT_NAME_SINGULAR,   // 'document'\n  });\n  const { openRecordInSidePanel } = useOpenRecordInSidePanel();\n  const { enqueueErrorSnackBar } = useSnackBar();\n\n  const createNewPage = useCallback(async () => {\n    const createPlan = buildNewPageCreatePlan();\n    try {\n      const createdRecord = await createOneRecord(createPlan.recordInput);\n      openRecordInSidePanel({ recordId: createdRecord.id, ... });\n      return createdRecord.id;\n    } catch {\n      enqueueErrorSnackBar({ message: t`Could not create the page. Please try again.` });\n      return null;\n    }\n  }, [...]);\n  return { createNewPage };\n};\n```\n\nNote how the caller must gate first: `useCreateNewPage` itself does not check installation; it assumes the object exists and catches the failure. The actual gate is in `NewPageHotKeyGate.tsx` (lines 26-30) and `useNewPageCommand.ts`, both of which check the a2e-documents universal identifier before this hook runs.\n\n### Summary of behavior for `a2eLink` if `a2e-links` is not installed\n\n- `useObjectMetadataItem({ objectNameSingular: 'a2eLink' })` → **throws `ObjectMetadataItemNotFoundError`**.\n- `useFindManyRecords({ objectNameSingular: 'a2eLink' })` → **throws** the same (skip does not help).\n- `useCreateOneRecord({ objectNameSingular: 'a2eLink' })` → **throws** the same at hook evaluation.\n- Therefore native front code must gate on `hasObjectMetadataItem(objectMetadataItems, 'a2eLink')` (object-presence pattern) **or** on the a2e-links universal identifier `895bb7aa-3ae3-400f-9dfa-72116f0021e2` via `applicationsSelector` (identifier pattern) before invoking these hooks — exactly as the existing document and invoice code does.\n\n---\n\n## File index (absolute paths)\n\nInstall state:\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/applications/states/applicationsSelector.ts`\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/applications/hooks/useInstalledApplications.ts`\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/applications/hooks/useIsThirdPartyApplication.ts`\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/applications/components/ApplicationsLoadEffect.tsx`\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/a2e-workspace/hooks/useA2eSuiteApplications.ts`\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/metadata-store/states/metadataStoreState.ts`\n\nObject