        "prompt": "In the twenty-front package of this repo (`packages/twenty-front/src`), I need a very thorough map of how command menu items / record actions are registered and rendered, including app-contributed ones. This is for implementing a \"Link…\" action on record pages and document pages.\n\nPlease find and report with exact file paths and line numbers:\n\n1. Where native command menu items are defined/registered (e.g. a command menu item registry, `CommandMenuItemDefinition`, engine components, `useCommandMenuItems`, etc.). How a developer adds a new native \"Link…\"-style command that appears in the Cmd+K command menu for a given object / record selection.\n\n2. How app-contributed command menu items (from `defineCommandMenuItem` app manifests, with `availabilityType: 'RECORD_SELECTION' | 'GLOBAL'`, `availabilityObjectUniversalIdentifier`, `frontComponentUniversalIdentifier`, `conditionalAvailabilityExpression`) are fetched and rendered in the command menu. What component renders a command menu item's front component? How does it pass context (record id, selected ids)?\n\n3. Whether command menu items can render interactive UI (not just a fire-and-unmount `Command`). Show any example of an app front component rendered in a side panel or modal from a command menu item (e.g. `CommandOpenSidePanelPage`, `openSidePanelPage`, `CommandModal`).\n\n4. The `SidePanelPages` enum and side panel page registry: how a side panel page/route is declared and what it takes to add a new one. Show `SidePanelSearchRecordsPage` and how it is registered.\n\n5. Any existing \"record action\" concept distinct from command menu (e.g. record show page action menu, `RecordShowPage` actions, `record-actions` module). Show how to mount an action/button on a record page header and on a document page.\n\nReport concrete code excerpts for the key seams. Be thorough; include the names of the exact functions/components/types I'd use. Do not write any code.",
