        "result": "<task id=\"ses_f074c4f82ffeB2TxjTcaVDsKYl\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nI have all the information needed. Let me compile the comprehensive report.\n\n---\n\n# Command Menu Items / Record Actions Map — `packages/twenty-front/src`\n\nThis repository does **not** have a client-side `CommandMenuItemDefinition` registry or `useCommandMenuItems` hook for *native* items. Native commands are **seeded server-side** as `commandMenuItem` metadata rows, fetched via GraphQL, filtered/rendered client-side. App-contributed items use the same pipeline plus a `frontComponent`. Here is the full seam map.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Where native command menu items are defined / registered\n\n### 1a. Server-side definition (the actual \"native registry\")\n\n**`packages/twenty-server/src/engine/workspace-manager/twenty-standard-application/constants/standard-command-menu-item.constant.ts`** (1492 lines) — this is the canonical registry of native commands. Each entry is an object: `universalIdentifier`, `label` (Lingui `msg`), `shortLabel`, `icon`, `position`, `isPinned`, `availabilityType`, `conditionalAvailabilityExpression`, `availabilityObjectMetadataUniversalIdentifier`, `frontComponentUniversalIdentifier` (always `null` for native), `engineComponentKey`, `hotKeys`.\n\nExample (lines 74–95, `deleteRecords`):\n```ts\ndeleteRecords: {\n  universalIdentifier: 'd5a55d57-ed1d-4791-89b8-53b7e121d69d',\n  label: i18nLabel(msg({ message: `Delete {objectLabel}`, context: 'commandMenuItem.label' })),\n  icon: 'IconTrash', isPinned: false, position: 4,\n  availabilityType: CommandMenuItemAvailabilityType.RECORD_SELECTION,\n  conditionalAvailabilityExpression:\n    'numberOfSelectedRecords >= 1 and not hasAnySoftDeleteFilterOnView and objectPermissions.canSoftDeleteObjectRecords and (isSelectAll or noneDefined(selectedRecords, \"deletedAt\"))',\n  engineComponentKey: EngineComponentKey.DELETE_RECORDS,\n  hotKeys: null,\n},\n```\n\nConsumed by:\n- **`.../utils/command-menu-item/create-standard-command-menu-item-flat-metadata.util.ts`** (lines 10–88) — turns a definition into a `FlatCommandMenuItem`, resolving `availabilityObjectMetadataUniversalIdentifier` to an id.\n- **`.../utils/command-menu-item/build-standard-flat-command-menu-item-maps.util.ts`** (lines 19–90) — iterates `STANDARD_COMMAND_MENU_ITEMS`, plus auto-generates one `NAVIGATION` item per active object.\n\nPer-object navigation commands are built in **`packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/flat-command-menu-item/utils/build-object-navigation-universal-flat-command-menu-item.util.ts`** (lines 70–127) and get their availability expression from `buildNavigationConditionalAvailabilityExpression` (lines 44–68).\n\nSeed front-component commands (dev samples) live in **`packages/twenty-server/src/engine/workspace-manager/standard-objects-prefill-data/utils/prefill-front-component-definitions.util.ts`** (`getSeedFrontComponentCommandMenuItemDefinitions`, lines 97–150) and **`prefill-front-component-command-menu-items.util.ts`**.\n\n### 1b. The engine component key enum (native command behaviour registry)\n\n**`packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/command-menu-item/enums/engine-component-key.enum.ts`** (lines 3–81) — `EngineComponentKey` (`NAVIGATION`, `DELETE_RECORDS`, `FRONT_COMPONENT_RENDERER`, `TRIGGER_WORKFLOW_VERSION`, `SEARCH_RECORDS`, `ASK_AI`, …). **Client-side map**: this exact enum appears in `~/generated-metadata/graphql`.\n\n### 1c. Client-side native command → React component map\n\n**`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/command-menu-item/engine-command/constants/EngineComponentKeyHeadlessComponentMap.tsx`** (lines 59–279) — `ENGINE_COMPONENT_KEY_COMPONENT_MAP: Record<EngineComponentKey, React.ReactNode>`. This is where you wire a `EngineComponentKey` to its command component. Examples:\n```ts\n[EngineComponentKey.DELETE_RECORDS]: <DeleteRecordsCommand />,\n[EngineComponentKey.NAVIGATION]: <NavigationEngineCommand />,\n[EngineComponentKey.SEARCH_RECORDS]: (\n  <HeadlessOpenSidePanelPageEngineCommand page={SidePanelPages.SearchRecords} pageTitle={msg`Search`} pageIcon={IconSearch} shouldResetSearchState={true} />\n),\n[EngineComponentKey.FRONT_COMPONENT_RENDERER]: <HeadlessFrontComponentRendererEngineCommand />,\n```\nNote the enum in `~/generated-metadata/graphql` is exhaustively mapped here — `assertUnreachable` is not used but every key must be present.\n\n### 1d. Mounting / running engine commands\n\n- **`.../engine-command/hooks/useMountCommand.ts`** (lines 14–88) — `useMountCommand()` builds a `HeadlessEngineCommandContextApi` (via `buildHeadlessCommandContextApi`) and stores it in `headlessCommandContextApisState` keyed by command item id. Optional `frontComponentId` / `workflowVersionId` enrichment.\n- **`.../engine-command/components/CommandRunner.tsx`** (lines 9–38) — reads `headlessCommandContextApisState`, wraps each in `ContextStoreComponentInstanceContext` + `CommandComponentInstanceContext` + `CommandMenuItemErrorBoundary`, and renders `ENGINE_COMPONENT_KEY_COMPONENT_MAP[context.engineComponentKey]`.\n- **`.../engine-command/components/HeadlessEngineCommandWrapperEffect.tsx`** (lines 15–63) — the fire-once-then-unmount pattern. **This is the seam for a fire-and-unmount native `Command`**: the command component calls `execute` once, then always `unmountCommand(commandMenuItemId)`.\n- **`.../engine-command/hooks/useUnmountEngineCommand.ts`**.\n- **`.../engine-command/types/HeadlessCommandContextApi.ts`** (lines 15–46) — the context passed to engine commands: `engineComponentKey`, `contextStoreInstanceId`, `objectMetadataItem`, `targetedRecordsRule`, `selectedRecords`, `payload`, `navigationTargetObjectMetadataId`, plus `HeadlessFrontComponentCommandContextApi` and `HeadlessTriggerWorkflowVersionCommandContextApi` variants.\n\n### 1e. How a developer adds a new *native* \"Link…\"-style command\n\nThere is no client-only registration. The flow is:\n1. Add an `EngineComponentKey` value in **`engine-component-key.enum.ts`** (`packages/twenty-server/.../command-menu-item/enums/engine-component-key.enum.ts`).\n2. Add an entry to **`standard-command-menu-item.constant.ts`** with `availabilityType`, `conditionalAvailabilityExpression`, and the new `engineComponentKey`.\n3. Map the key to a React command component in **`EngineComponentKeyHeadlessComponentMap.tsx`**.\n4. Implement the command component (e.g. copy-link-to-page) using `HeadlessEngineCommandWrapperEffect` for fire-and-unmount, or render interactive UI.\n\nFor a **native client-only** alternative (no metadata seeding), see the app-action pattern in **`.../display/hooks/useCommandMenuAppActions.ts`** (lines 36–58), which builds pseudo-items like `copy-page-link` with `id`, `label`, `Icon`, `onClick`, `isAvailable` and renders them directly in `SidePanelCommandMenuItemDisplayPage.tsx` (lines 174–194). Note the existing `'copy-page-link'` action (`t\\`Copy link to page\\``, lines 44–50) — a direct precedent for a \"Link…\" action, though it currently lives only in the Cmd+K list.\n\n### 1f. Full rendering pipeline (fetch → filter → render)\n\n- **`.../graphql/queries/findManyCommandMenuItems.ts`** — `FIND_MANY_COMMAND_MENU_ITEMS`. Fragment: **`.../graphql/fragments/commandMenuItemFragment.ts`** (fields: `id, universalIdentifier, applicationId, frontComponentId, frontComponent { id name isHeadless }, engineComponentKey, label, icon, shortLabel, position, isPinned, payload{...on PathCommandMenuItemPayload{path}}, hotKeys, conditionalAvailabilityExpression, availabilityType, availabilityObjectMetadataId, navigationTargetObjectMetadataId, pageLayoutId, isActive`).\n- **`.../states/commandMenuItemsSelector.ts`** (lines 8–36) — reads from `metadataStoreState` (`commandMenuItems` + `frontComponents`), filters `isActive`, joins `frontComponent`.\n- **`.../contexts/CommandMenuContextProvider.tsx`** (lines 17–61) — picks normal vs `CommandMenuContextProviderWithWorkflowEnrichment`, computes `commandMenuContextApi` via `useCurrentCommandMenuContextApi()`.\n- **`.../contexts/CommandMenuContextProviderContent.tsx`** (lines 28–90) — the **filter chain**:\n  ```ts\n  .filter(doesCommandMenuItemMatchObjectMetadataId(currentObjectMetadataItemId))\n  .filter(doesCommandMenuItemMatchPageType(commandMenuContextApi.pageType))\n  .filter(doesCommandMenuItemMatchSelectionState(hasSelectedRecords))\n  .filter(doesCommandMenuItemMatchPageLayoutId(effectivePageLayoutId))\n  .filter((item) => evaluateConditionalAvailabilityExpression(item.conditionalAvailabilityExpression, commandMenuContextApi))\n  .sort((a, b) => a.position - b.position);\n  ```\n  Filter utils live in `.../utils/doesCommandMenuItemMatchObjectMetadataId.ts`, `doesCommandMenuItemMatchPageType.ts`, `doesCommandMenuItemMatchSelectionState.ts`, `doesCommandMenuItemMatchPageLayoutId.ts`.\n- **`.../display/components/CommandMenuItemRenderer.tsx`** (lines 39–205) — the actual renderer. `CommandMenuItemButtonRenderer` (displayType `button`, uses `CommandMenuButton`) and `CommandMenuItemSelectableRenderer` (`listItem`/`dropdownItem`, uses `CommandMenuItem` / `MenuItem` / `AppMenuItem` for third-party apps). Labels/icons interpolated via `interpolateCommandMenuItemFields` (line 48) and click behaviour from `useCommandMenuItemClick` (line 55).\n- **`.../display/components/PinnedCommandMenuItemButtons.tsx`** (lines 49–161) — pinned header buttons; `containerType === SidePanelFooter` controls label placement.\n\n### 1g. Context the renderer receives\n\n- **`.../contexts/CommandMenuContext.ts`** (lines 7–21) — `{ displayType, containerType, commandMenuItems, commandMenuContextApi, isInPreviewMode }`.\n- **`packages/twenty-shared/src/types/CommandMenuContextApi.ts`** (lines 5–24) — `pageType`, `isInSidePanel`, `selectedRecords: ObjectRecord[]`, `numberOfSelectedRecords`, `isSelectAll`, `objectPermissions`, `objectMetadataItem`, `objectMetadataLabel`, `featureFlags`, `permissionFlags`, `targetObjectReadPermissions`, `targetObjectWritePermissions`, etc.\n- **`.../hooks/useCurrentCommandMenuContextApi.ts`** (lines 34–205) — builds that context from ContextStore. Selected record ids come from `contextStoreTargetedRecordsRuleComponentState` (`mode === 'selection'` → `selectedRecordIds`); records resolved via `recordStoreRecordsSelector` (line 77).\n- **`.../types/CommandMenuItemContainerType.ts`** (lines 1–10) — `CommandMenuList`, `IndexPageHeader`, `IndexPageDropdown`, `ShowPageHeader`, `StandalonePageHeader`, `CommandMenuShowPageDropdown`, `SidePanelFooter`, `WidgetHeader`.\n\n### 1h. Cmd+K host\n\n- **`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/command-menu/hooks/useCommandMenuHotKeys.ts`** (lines 22–30) — `ctrl+k`/`meta+k` → `toggleSidePanelMenu()`.\n- **`.../side-panel/hooks/useSidePanelMenu.ts`** (lines 63–101) — opens `SidePanelPages.CommandMenuDisplay`.\n- **`.../side-panel/constants/SidePanelPagesConfig.tsx`** (line 47) — maps `CommandMenuDisplay` → `SidePanelCommandMenuItemDisplayPage`.\n- **`.../command-menu-item/display/components/SidePanelCommandMenuItemDisplayPage.tsx`** (lines 149–206) — the Cmd+K list; renders pinned/other/fallback groups of `CommandMenuItemRenderer`, plus `TemplatesCommand`, `QuickCaptureCommand`, `NewPageCommand`, and `useCommandMenuAppActions()` items.\n- Mobile: **`.../command-menu/components/CommandMenuForMobile.tsx`** (lines 15–34) portals `SidePanelRouter` into `CommandMenuOpenContainer`.\n\n---\n\n## 2. App-contributed command menu items\n\n**App manifest definition** — **`packages/twenty-sdk/src/sdk/define/command-menu-items/define-command-menu-item.ts`** (lines 5–32). Validates `universalIdentifier`, `label`, and **`frontComponentUniversalIdentifier`** (required). Config type: **`command-menu-item-config.ts`** — `CommandMenuItemConfig = Omit<CommandMenuItemManifest, 'conditionalAvailabilityExpression'> & { conditionalAvailabilityExpression?: boolean | string }`.\n\nReal example — **`packages/twenty-apps/examples/document-generator/src/command-menu-items/generate-document.command-menu-item.ts`** (lines 13–23):\n```ts\nexport default defineCommandMenuItem({\n  universalIdentifier: GENERATE_DOCUMENT_COMMAND_UNIVERSAL_IDENTIFIER,\n  label: 'Generate document', shortLabel: 'Generate', isPinned: false,\n  availabilityType: 'RECORD_SELECTION',\n  availabilityObjectUniversalIdentifier:\n    STANDARD_OBJECT_UNIVERSAL_IDENTIFIERS.person.universalIdentifier,\n  frontComponentUniversalIdentifier:\n    GENERATE_DOCUMENT_FORM_FRONT_COMPONENT_UNIVERSAL_IDENTIFIER,\n});\n```\n`STANDARD_OBJECT_UNIVERSAL_IDENTIFIERS` is re-exported by **`packages/twenty-sdk/src/sdk/define/objects/standard-object-ids.ts`** (line 1) and **`packages/twenty-sdk/src/sdk/define/index.ts`** (lines 133–134).\n\n**Server conversion** — **`packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/application/application-manifest/converters/from-command-menu-item-manifest-to-universal-flat-command-menu-item.util.ts`** (lines 7–44). Key point (line 33):\n```ts\nengineComponentKey: EngineComponentKey.FRONT_COMPONENT_RENDERER,\nfrontComponentUniversalIdentifier: commandMenuItemManifest.frontComponentUniversalIdentifier,\navailabilityObjectMetadataUniversalIdentifier: commandMenuItemManifest.availabilityObjectUniversalIdentifier ?? null,\navailabilityType: commandMenuItemManifest.availabilityType ?? CommandMenuItemAvailabilityType.GLOBAL,\n```\nSo **every app-contributed item is `FRONT_COMPONENT_RENDERER`** with a `frontComponentId`.\n\n**Fetch/render** — same `FIND_MANY_COMMAND_MENU_ITEMS` → `commandMenuItemsSelector` → `CommandMenuContextProviderContent` filter chain as native items. `availabilityObjectUniversalIdentifier` becomes `availabilityObjectMetadataId` and is matched by `doesCommandMenuItemMatchObjectMetadataId`.\n\n**Click dispatch** — **`.../hooks/useCommandMenuItemClick.ts`** (lines 17–125). The crucial branch (lines 44–116):\n- `isHeadless` = `frontComponentId` present && `frontComponent.isHeadless === true` → `mountCommand({... frontComponentId ...})` (renders via `HeadlessFrontComponentRendererEngineCommand` → `FrontComponentRenderer`, mounted in `CommandRunner`, auto-unmounts on completion).\n- `isEngineCommand` = `engineComponentKey` present && no `frontComponentId` → `mountCommand`.\n- `isFrontComponent` = `frontComponentId` present && not headless → **opens in side panel**:\n```ts\nconst { selectedRecords, objectMetadataItem } = commandMenuContextApi;\nconst recordId = selectedRecords.length === 1 ? selectedRecords[0].id : undefined;\nconst objectNameSingular = objectMetadataItem.nameSingular as string | undefined;\ncloseCommandMenu();\nopenFrontComponentInSidePanel({\n  frontComponentId: item.frontComponentId,\n  pageTitle: label,\n  pageIcon: Icon,\n  recordContext: isDefined(recordId) && isDefined(objectNameSingular)\n    ? { recordId, objectNameSingular } : undefined,\n});\n```\n\n**What renders the front component** — **`.../front-components/components/FrontComponentRenderer.tsx`** (lines 46–201). Props (lines 25–32): `frontComponentId`, `commandMenuItemId?`, `selectedRecordIds?: string[]`, `timelineActivityId?`, `loadingFallback?`, `unavailableFallback?`. It fetches via `FindOneFrontComponentDocument`, computes an `executionContext` + `frontComponentHostCommunicationApi` from **`.../front-components/hooks/useFrontComponentExecutionContext.ts`**, and renders `SharedFrontComponentRenderer` from `twenty-front-component-renderer`.\n\n**How context (record id / selected ids) is passed** — **`useFrontComponentExecutionContext.ts`** (lines 438–448):\n```ts\nconst executionContext: FrontComponentExecutionContext = {\n  frontComponentId,\n  userId: currentUser?.id ?? null,\n  recordId: selectedRecordIds?.length === 1 ? selectedRecordIds[0] : null,\n  selectedRecordIds: selectedRecordIds ?? [],\n  timelineActivityId: timelineActivityId ?? null,\n  colorScheme,\n  locale: i18n.locale as AppLocale,\n};\n```\nFor record-page side-panel rendering, **`.../side-panel/pages/front-component/components/SidePanelFrontComponentPage.tsx`** (lines 15–43) reads `viewableFrontComponentIdComponentState` + `viewableFrontComponentRecordContextComponentState`, converts to `selectedRecordIds = [recordContext.recordId]`, and passes to `FrontComponentRenderer`. Those states are set by **`.../side-panel/hooks/useOpenFrontComponentInSidePanel.ts`** (lines 31–51).\n\nNote: `CommandMenuItemAvailabilityType` (shared, **`packages/twenty-shared/src/types/CommandMenuItemAvailabilityType.ts`**, lines 1–6) is `GLOBAL | GLOBAL_OBJECT_CONTEXT | RECORD_SELECTION | FALLBACK`.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Can command items render interactive UI (not just fire-and-unmount)?\n\n**Yes**, via three distinct mechanisms:\n\n**(a) Front component in side panel** — `useCommandMenuItemClick` → `openFrontComponentInSidePanel` (above), rendered by `SidePanelFrontComponentPage` → `FrontComponentRenderer`. This is the standard interactive UI for app commands. Example app: `packages/twenty-apps/examples/document-generator/.../generate-document.command-menu-item.ts` opens a form in the side panel.\n\n**(b) `CommandOpenSidePanelPage` equivalent — `HeadlessOpenSidePanelPageEngineCommand`** — **`.../engine-command/components/HeadlessOpenSidePanelPageEngineCommand.tsx`** (lines 10–37). A native engine command that calls `navigateSidePanel({ page, pageTitle, pageIcon })`. Used by `SEARCH_RECORDS`, `ASK_AI` (see `EngineComponentKeyHeadlessComponentMap.tsx` lines 198–219). The full side-panel navigation hook is `useNavigateSidePanel` (**`.../side-panel/hooks/useNavigateSidePanel.ts`**, lines 62–116).\n\n**(c) Confirmation modal** — **`.../command-menu-item/confirmation-modal/components/CommandMenuConfirmationModalManager.tsx`** (lines 18–87) and **`.../confirmation-modal/hooks/useCommandMenuConfirmationModal.ts`** (lines 13–47). Front components can request a modal via the host API method `openCommandConfirmationModal` (see `useFrontComponentExecutionContext.ts` lines 390–404 and `openConfirmationModal`), and the result is emitted as a browser `CustomEvent` (`COMMAND_MENU_CONFIRMATION_MODAL_RESULT_BROWSER_EVENT_NAME`). This is the \"`CommandModal`\" equivalent. There is no component literally named `CommandOpenSidePanelPage`/`CommandModal` in the codebase.\n\n**Headless vs interactive distinction** in click handling (`useCommandMenuItemClick.ts` lines 44–55):\n```ts\nconst isHeadless = isDefined(item.frontComponentId) && item.frontComponent?.isHeadless === true;\nconst isEngineCommand = isDefined(item.engineComponentKey) && !isDefined(item.frontComponentId);\nconst isFrontComponent = isDefined(item.frontComponentId) && item.frontComponent?.isHeadless !== true;\nconst shouldMountCommand = isHeadless || isEngineCommand;\n```\n\nAlso relevant: `HeadlessEngineCommandWrapperEffect` (fire-and-unmount), `HeadlessFrontComponentRendererEngineCommand` (**`.../engine-command/components/HeadlessFrontComponentRendererEngineCommand.tsx`**, lines 14–38 — headless front component mounted inline, receives `commandMenuItemId` + `selectedRecordIds`), `HeadlessOpenAiChatHistoryTabEngineCommand`, `HeadlessNavigateEngineCommand`.\n\n---\n\n## 4. `SidePanelPages` enum and side panel page registry\n\n**Enum** — **`packages/twenty-shared/src/types/SidePanelPages.ts`** (lines 1–51), re-exported from `packages/twenty-shared/src/types/index.ts` (line 316). Includes `SearchRecords = 'search-records'` (line 19), `ViewFrontComponent = 'view-front-component'` (line 29), `RoutedPage` (42), `QuickCapture` (47), `TemplateGallery` (50), etc. Several are marked deprecated (`ViewRecord`, `ViewRecords`, `Copilot`).\n\n**Page type guards** — **`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/side-panel/types/SidePanelPage.ts`** (lines 1–15): `PurposeBuiltSidePanelPage = Exclude<SidePanelPages, LegacySidePanelPage | RoutedPage>`; `ActiveSidePanelPage = PurposeBuiltSidePanelPage | RoutedPage`.\n\n**Registry** — **`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/side-panel/constants/SidePanelPagesConfig.tsx`** (lines 43–116):\n```ts\nexport const SIDE_PANEL_PAGES_CONFIG = new Map<ActiveSidePanelPage, React.ReactNode>([\n  ...\n  [SidePanelPages.SearchRecords, <SidePanelSearchRecordsPage />],  // line 61\n  [SidePanelPages.ViewFrontComponent, <SidePanelFrontComponentPage />],  // line 89\n  ...\n]);\n```\n\n**Router** — **`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/side-panel/components/SidePanelRouter.tsx`** (lines 33–141). Reads `sidePanelNavigationStackState`, gets `SIDE_PANEL_PAGES_CONFIG.get(sidePanelPage)`, clones with `key: sidePanelPageInstanceId`, and wraps in `SidePanelPageComponentInstanceContext` + `WorkspaceSurfaceContext` + a `CommandMenuContextProvider displayType=\"listItem\" containerType={CommandMenuList}`.\n\n**`SidePanelSearchRecordsPage`** — **`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/side-panel/pages/search/components/SidePanelSearchRecordsPage.tsx`** (lines 45–233). It composes `useSidePanelSearchRecords`, `useAppSearchResultItems`, `useChatSearchResultItems`, `useDriveSearchResultItems`, `useHelpSearchResultItems`, groups results with `groupSearchResultItems`, and renders rows with `CommandMenuItem` inside `SelectableListItem`. Its openers: **`useOpenRecordsSearchPageInSidePanel.ts`** (lines 9–26) and `HeadlessOpenSidePanelPageEngineCommand` (in `EngineComponentKeyHeadlessComponentMap.tsx` lines 198–212).\n\n**To add a new side panel page**: add a value to the `SidePanelPages` enum (shared package), create the page component, register it in `SIDE_PANEL_PAGES_CONFIG`, then open it via `useNavigateSidePanel().navigateSidePanel({ page, pageTitle, pageIcon })` (or `useSidePanelMenu().navigateSidePanelMenu`). `HeadlessOpenSidePanelPageEngineCommand` wraps that for engine commands.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Record-action concept distinct from command menu\n\nThere **is no** separate `record-actions` module or `RecordShowPage` action registry. \"Record actions\" in this repo means either:\n\n**(a) The command menu item itself, mounted on record pages.** The record show page hosts command items in its header via **`packages/twenty-front/src/pages/object-record/RecordShowPage.tsx`** (lines 94–128):\n```tsx\n<RecordShowPageHeader objectNameSingular={...} objectRecordId={...}>\n  {!isInSidePanel && (\n    <>\n      <RecordShowCommandMenu />\n      {!isLayoutCustomizationModeEnabled && <SidePanelToggleButton />}\n    </>\n  )}\n</RecordShowPageHeader>\n```\n**`packages/twenty-front/src/pages/object-record/RecordShowPageHeader.tsx`** (lines 20–84) — `RecordShowPageMainHeader` passes `actionButton={children}` to `PageCardHeader`; `RecordShowPagePanelHeader` (side-panel variant) has no action button.\n\n**`.../command-menu-item/components/RecordShowCommandMenu.tsx`** (lines 12–47) — renders pinned command items as header buttons using `CommandMenuContextProvider displayType=\"button\" containerType={ShowPageHeader}` → `PinnedCommandMenuItemButtons`, plus `CommandMenuItemEditButton`. **This is exactly where a new record-page action/button appears if the item is `isPinned` + `RECORD_SELECTION`.**\n\nInside the side panel, **`.../object-record/record-show/components/PageLayoutRecordPageRenderer.tsx`** (lines 99–107) renders a `SidePanelFooter` with `RecordPageSidePanelCommandMenu`, `RecordPageSidePanelWidgetCommandMenuItems`, and `RecordPageSidePanelPinnedCommandMenuItems`.\n\n**(b) The record page dropdown action menu** — **`.../command-menu-item/components/RecordPageSidePanelCommandMenu.tsx`** (lines 7–26, `displayType=\"dropdownItem\"`, container `CommandMenuShowPageDropdown`) → **`RecordPageSidePanelCommandMenuDropdown.tsx`** (lines 17–114), which filters `availabilityType === RECORD_SELECTION` (lines 38–46) and renders `CommandMenuItemRenderer` rows inside `OptionsDropdownMenu`.\n\n**(c) A distinct \"related record action\" API for widget/page-layout actions** (not the Cmd+K menu):\n- **`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/activities/types/RelatedRecordAction.ts`**\n- **`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/activities/hooks/useRelatedRecordActions.ts`**\n- Concrete actions: `useComposeCalendarEventRelatedRecordAction.ts`, `useComposeEmailRelatedRecordAction.ts`, `useAttachFileRelatedRecordAction.tsx`, `useCreateActivityRelatedRecordAction.ts`\n- Widget wrappers: `.../page-layout/widgets/components/WidgetActionRelatedRecord.tsx`, `WidgetActionActivityCreate.tsx`, `.../emails/components/WidgetActionEmailCompose.tsx`, `.../files/components/WidgetActionFileAttach.tsx`, `.../calendar/components/WidgetActionCalendarEventCreate.tsx`, `.../timeline/components/WidgetActionTimelineCreateRelated.tsx`.\n\n**(d) Document/standalone page actions** — a document (page-layout) header mounts command items via **`packages/twenty-front/src/pages/page-layout/StandalonePageHeader.tsx`** (lines 16–47):\n```tsx\n<PageCardHeader icon={...} title={title}\n  actionButton={<><StandalonePageCommandMenu />{!isLayoutCustomizationModeEnabled && <SidePanelToggleButton />}</>} />\n```\n**`.../command-menu-item/components/StandalonePageCommandMenu.tsx`** (lines 25–140) is the standalone-page analogue: it builds its own `CommandMenuContextApi` with `pageType: ContextStorePageType.Standalone`, `selectedRecords: []`, then filters `commandMenuItems` with `doesCommandMenuItemMatchObjectMetadataId(undefined)`, excludes `RECORD_SELECTION`/`GLOBAL_OBJECT_CONTEXT`, applies `doesCommandMenuItemMatchPageLayoutId(currentPageLayoutId)` and `evaluateConditionalAvailabilityExpression`, and renders `PinnedCommandMenuItemButtons`. This is the seam for a document-page \"Link…\" action — an item with `pageLayoutId` set and `GLOBAL`/`FALLBACK` availability appears here.\n\n---\n\n## Key seams summary for a \"Link…\" action\n\n| Concern | File |\n|---|---|\n| Native command registry (server) | `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/workspace-manager/twenty-standard-application/constants/standard-command-menu-item.constant.ts` |\n| Engine key enum (server) | `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/command-menu-item/enums/engine-component-key.enum.ts` |\n| Native key → component map (client) | `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/command-menu-item/engine-command/constants/EngineComponentKeyHeadlessComponentMap.tsx` |\n| Fire-and-unmount wrapper | `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/command-menu-item/engine-command/components/HeadlessEngineCommandWrapperEffect.tsx` |\n| Command mount/context | `.../engine-command/hooks/useMountCommand.ts`, `.../engine-command/components/CommandRunner.tsx` |\n| Client-side quick actions (no metadata) | `.../display/hooks/useCommandMenuAppActions.ts` (existing `copy-page-link`) |\n| Click dispatch | `.../hooks/useCommandMenuItemClick.ts` |\n| Item renderer | `.../display/components/CommandMenuItemRenderer.tsx` |\n| Filter chain | `.../contexts/CommandMenuContextProviderContent.tsx` |\n| Context API type | `packages/twenty-shared/src/types/CommandMenuContextApi.ts` |\n| Context builder | `.../hooks/useCurrentCommandMenuContextApi.ts` |\n| App manifest define | `packages/twenty-sdk/src/sdk/define/command-menu-items/define-command-menu-item.ts` |\n| Manifest → flat converter | `packages/twenty-server/.../application-manifest/converters/from-command-menu-item-manifest-to-universal-flat-command-menu-item.util.ts` |\n| Front component renderer | `.../front-components/components/FrontComponentRenderer.tsx` |\n| Front component context/host API | `.../front-components/hooks/useFrontComponentExecutionContext.ts` |\n| Side panel enum | `packages/twenty-shared/src/types/SidePanelPages.ts` |\n| Side panel registry | `.../side-panel/constants/SidePanelPagesConfig.tsx` |\n| Side panel router | `.../side-panel/components/SidePanelRouter.tsx` |\n| Side panel navigation | `.../side-panel/hooks/useNavigateSidePanel.ts`, `useSidePanelMenu.ts` |\n| Open front component in panel | `.../side-panel/hooks/useOpenFrontComponentInSidePanel.ts` + `.../pages/front-component/components/SidePanelFrontComponentPage.tsx` |\n| Record page header/actions | `packages/twenty-front/src/pages/object-record/RecordShowPage.tsx`, `RecordShowPageHeader.tsx`, `.../command-menu-item/components/RecordShowCommandMenu.tsx` |\n| Document/standalone page actions | `packages/twenty-front/src/pages/page-layout/StandalonePageHeader.tsx`, `.../command-menu-item/components/StandalonePageCommandMenu.tsx` |\n| Confirmation modal | `.../command-menu-item/confirmation-modal/components/CommandMenuConfirmationModalManager.tsx`, `.../hooks/useCommandMenuConfirmationModal.ts` |\n\n**Important architectural note:** unlike the rest of the codebase, there is *no* `CommandMenuItemDefinition` type or `useCommandMenuItems` hook client-side — those names live only in `packages/twenty-sdk` (`DefineEntity`) and server conversions. Native items are persisted metadata; the client is purely fetch/filter/render. Adding a native command therefore requires a server constant entry + enum value + a client map entry. A purely front-end \"Link…\" action can instead follow `useCommandMenuAppActions` (like `copy-page-link`) or be an app-contributed front component.\n</task_result>\n</task>"
